Key Terms:
- GPU: A processor designed for many parallel calculations, including graphics work.
- AI Accelerator: Specialized hardware that can speed up certain AI calculations.
- Parallel Processing: Performing multiple operations at the same time.

8. Sensors, Actuators, and Microcontrollers:

Goal:
To help beginners understand how a machine can sense the physical world, make a decision with a tiny computer, and act on that decision, using one robot example from start to finish.

Learning Objectives:
Students will be able to:
- Explain the difference between a sensor and an actuator, and give examples of each.
- Describe how a sensor signal becomes numbers a computer can use (sampling, quantization, encoding).
- Explain what a microcontroller is and how it differs from a general-purpose computer such as a laptop.
- Describe the sense–decide–act loop of a simple robot.
- Calculate a distance from the echo time of an ultrasonic sensor.
- Trace the program of an obstacle-avoiding robot and predict what it will do.

